So if you're done with your
little nostalgic moment,


00:55:57.664 --> 00:55:59.154
maybe you can think a little bit


00:55:59.266 --> 00:56:02.497
and help me catch these guys.


00:56:02.602 --> 00:56:03.830
Just help me.


00:56:03.937 --> 00:56:06.565
Just put yourself in their shoes.


00:56:06.673 --> 00:56:09.699
- Come on. If this were your fire sale,
- Okay, okay.


00:56:09.809 --> 00:56:13.074
- you were running this thing, what would be your next move?
- Okay, uh...


00:56:13.179 --> 00:56:15.147
Well, the whole point of a fire sale


00:56:15.248 --> 00:56:17.216
is that it-it's mostly
done by remote, right?


00:56:17.317 --> 00:56:22.755
But... but not everything is run completely
online. Uh, uh, major utilities aren't.


00:56:22.856 --> 00:56:27.520
They're run by closed-circuit, so you could
breach the security up to a certain point, but, um,


00:56:27.627 --> 00:56:29.822
to shut it down, you would
have to physically go there.


00:56:29.930 --> 00:56:31.761
You'd have to show up,
right, and-and, uh...


00:56:31.865 --> 00:56:34.390
You know what? Give me that guy's P.D.A.


00:56:34.501 --> 00:56:36.059
The phones don't work. They're all dead.


00:56:36.169 --> 00:56:38.228
No, the phones are fine;
it's the network that's dead.


00:56:38.338 --> 00:56:40.203
I've just got to reprogram it


00:56:40.307 --> 00:56:41.740
and link it into the old SATCOMs.


00:56:41.841 --> 00:56:42.773
Hackers surf'em


00:56:42.876 --> 00:56:44.207
all the time... that's probably


00:56:44.311 --> 00:56:45.369
what these guys are using


00:56:45.478 --> 00:56:46.376
to talk to each other.


00:56:46.479 --> 00:56:47.571
How do you know all this stuff?


00:56:47.681 --> 00:56:49.308
Dude, I don't know.


00:56:49.416 --> 00:56:51.350
There's a lot rattling around up there.


00:56:51.451 --> 00:56:52.679
I couldn't tell you.


00:56:52.786 --> 00:56:55.550
Okay. National power grid... uh,


00:56:55.655 --> 00:56:57.555
gas and electric is divided
into three zones, right?


00:56:57.657 --> 00:57:00.558
Eastern, central and western,
each with a primary hub.


00:57:01.978 --> 00:57:03.912
Here it is.


00:57:04.014 --> 00:57:05.481
What is that?


00:57:05.582 --> 00:57:07.982
- What are we looking at?
- That is the eastern hub.


00:57:08.084 --> 00:57:10.075
Now, they take this out...


00:57:10.186 --> 00:57:13.553
wipes out all the power for
the entire eastern corridor.


00:57:13.657 --> 00:57:15.488
But again, you'd have to do it manually.


00:57:15.592 --> 00:57:18.891
Okay... Come on. Let's go.


00:57:18.995 --> 00:57:20.292
What, to West Virginia?


00:57:20.397 --> 00:57:21.796
Hey, l-I honestly don't think


00:57:21.898 --> 00:57:24.093
I can handle any more
people trying to kill me.


00:57:24.200 --> 00:57:25.224
McClane? McClane?


00:57:25.335 --> 00:57:26.802
McClane... Oh, shit.


00:57:26.903 --> 00:57:28.063
Sir, wireless networks are down,


00:57:28.171 --> 00:57:29.536
and I think they're
hitting the landlines, too.


00:57:31.225 --> 00:57:34.626
I don't care how. You find me a line.


00:57:34.728 --> 00:57:36.320
Come on. Whatcha got?


00:57:36.429 --> 00:57:38.954
We swept the whole building.
Seems clean. We can sweep it again.


00:57:39.065 --> 00:57:42.159
- I don't think we're gonna find anything.
- Don't bother. Don't bother.


00:57:42.268 --> 00:57:44.065
It's a fake.


00:57:44.170 --> 00:57:45.762
This guy's playing us.


00:57:45.872 --> 00:57:48.898
Okay, get everyone back
inside the crisis center now.


00:57:49.009 --> 00:57:50.772
Okay. Let's open it up!


00:57:53.062 --> 00:57:54.962
Come on. Get in.


00:57:55.064 --> 00:57:57.123
Door's locked,


00:57:57.232 --> 00:57:59.632
unless you have an extra
gun I can use to unlock it.


00:58:01.737 --> 00:58:05.571
Hey, hey, don't do that.
Hey! You're gonna disable it.


00:58:06.508 --> 00:58:08.305
Jesus Christ!


00:58:08.410 --> 00:58:10.640
Oh! That was crazy. Did you see that?


00:58:10.746 --> 00:58:12.145
Sorry about that, man.


00:58:12.247 --> 00:58:14.875
I didn't know it would come out so fast.


00:58:16.785 --> 00:58:19.185
Uh... man...


00:58:19.288 --> 00:58:20.653
How'd you do yours?


00:58:23.058 --> 00:58:24.286
You all right?


00:58:24.393 --> 00:58:28.295
What'd you...? What, it
hit you a little bit? Sorry.


00:58:31.033 --> 00:58:32.625
Oh, no, listen, do-do not...


00:58:32.735 --> 00:58:35.568
Please don't touch those, okay? I know
what I'm doing. I've done this before.


00:58:35.671 --> 00:58:37.866
I mean, l-I've read about it.


00:58:37.973 --> 00:58:41.704
Road assist, we've detected
an air bag deployment.


00:58:41.810 --> 00:58:44.244
Yes, um... Please, we just hit a tree,


00:58:44.346 --> 00:58:46.473
and my-my my dad is
having a heart attack.


00:58:46.582 --> 00:58:48.743
And I think he's gonna
die! You need to help us.


00:58:48.851 --> 00:58:51.718
Hold while we contact
emergency services.


00:58:51.820 --> 00:58:53.811
No, no, no, he's... he's dying.


00:58:53.922 --> 00:58:56.083
Please, listen to me. l-I
can get him to a hospital.


00:58:56.191 --> 00:58:57.453
I can drive. I'm fine.


00:58:57.559 --> 00:58:58.924
But I can't really turn the key.


00:58:59.028 --> 00:59:01.155
The key won't start, so you gotta start


00:59:01.263 --> 00:59:02.855
the car for us, okay? Please, Dad...


00:59:02.965 --> 00:59:04.023
Your name, please?


00:59:04.133 --> 00:59:05.293
Uh...


00:59:05.401 --> 00:59:07.961
my name is-is...


00:59:08.070 --> 00:59:09.298
Frank...


00:59:09.405 --> 00:59:11.703
and my dad's name is,


00:59:11.807 --> 00:59:13.069
um...


00:59:13.175 --> 00:59:15.370
is...


00:59:15.477 --> 00:59:18.640
"Dvorak Tsarjenski."


00:59:19.681 --> 00:59:20.909
Please...


00:59:21.016 --> 00:59:23.280
Please just help us, okay?
We need your help, please!


00:59:23.385 --> 00:59:26.115
Emergency services are on their way.


00:59:26.221 --> 00:59:27.518
No, no, h-hold on. Listen to me.


00:59:27.623 --> 00:59:29.147
Listen to me, ma'am. What is your name?


00:59:29.258 --> 00:59:30.885
- Dolores.
- Dolores?


00:59:30.993 --> 00:59:34.190
Okay, Dolores, uh, I don't know
if you have a dad, but I do,


00:59:34.296 --> 00:59:36.821
and I want to be able to say
that a year from now, okay?


00:59:36.932 --> 00:59:38.365
Because my dad is my hero,


00:59:38.467 --> 00:59:40.697
and right now he is in my arms dying.


00:59:40.803 --> 00:59:44.102
A-And his only hope i-is to
get to a hospital right now.


00:59:44.206 --> 00:59:47.334
And we can't wait, so
please start the goddamn car!


00:59:51.480 --> 00:59:53.675
Thank you, Dolores.


00:59:53.782 --> 00:59:56.148
Pass me the P.D.A. I
gotta call the Warlock.


00:59:56.251 --> 00:59:57.479
- The what?
- The Warlock.


00:59:57.586 --> 00:59:59.850
He's a digitalJedi. He's amazing.


01:00:17.706 --> 01:00:19.037
Ma'am, you're not authorized to be here.


01:00:19.141 --> 01:00:21.837
F.B.I. We suspect there's
been a security breach.


01:00:21.944 --> 01:00:24.344
No, you can't land here
without authoriza...

